    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA7:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "the king said to Nathan the prophet, “See now, I dwell in a house of cedar, but God’s ark dwells within curtains.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA7:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nathan said to the king, “Go, do all that is in your heart, for the LORD is with you.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA7:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "That same night, the LORD’s word came to Nathan, saying,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA7:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nathan spoke to David all these words, and according to all this vision."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA12:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD sent Nathan to David. He came to him, and said to him, “There were two men in one city: the one rich, and the other poor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA12:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "David’s anger burned hot against the man, and he said to Nathan, “As the LORD lives, the man who has done this deserves to die!"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA12:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nathan said to David, “You are the man! This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘I anointed you king over Israel, and I delivered you out of the hand of Saul."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA12:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said to Nathan, “I have sinned against the LORD.” Nathan said to David, “The LORD also has put away your sin. You will not die."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA12:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Nathan departed to his house. The LORD struck the child that Uriah’s wife bore to David, and he was very sick."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA12:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "and he sent by the hand of Nathan the prophet, and he named him Jedidiah, for the LORD’s sake."
      }
    ],
